{"name":"Badass Grass","hex":"#b4da55","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"badass","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A belligerent or mean person; a person with an unpleasantly extreme appearance, attitudes, or behavior.","A person considered impressive due to courage, skill, daring, audacity, and/or toughness."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Belligerent and troublesome.","Having an extreme appearance, attitude, or behavior that is considered admirable."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/badass"},{"term":"grass","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any plant of the family Poaceae, characterized by leaves that arise from nodes in the stem and leaf bases that wrap around the stem, especially those grown as ground cover rather than for grain.","Any of the various plants that are not in the family Poaceae that resemble grasses."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To lay out on the grass; to knock down (an opponent etc.).","To act as a grass or informer, to betray; to report on (criminals etc) to the authorities."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grass"}],"entries":[{"title":"Grass","blocks":[{"text":"Grass refers to various families of plants. The three major families of grasslike plants are true grasses (Poaceae), sedges (Cyperaceae), and rushes (Juncaceae). Lawns and pasturelands are typically composed of true grasses, five of which cover 46% of the world's arable land: rice, wheat, maize, barley, and sugar cane."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Poa_annua.jpg/330px-Poa_annua.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grass","wikidata":"Q643352"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"badass":[{"type":"audio/flac","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/cc/En-us-badass.flac?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wik